<title>USA: TABLE-Pronet Q2 loss narrows/wins contract.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Pronet Q2 loss narrows/wins contract.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pronet Inc</p>
<p>			  Three Months Ended     Six Months Ended</p>
<p>				 June 30,		  June 30,</p>
<p>			     1997	 1996	 1997	 1996</p>
<p>Total Revenues	 $30,059     24,815     58,992     48,977</p>
<p>Operating (loss)    (15,962)   (10,246)   (24,780)   (12,738)</p>
<p>Net Loss		(20,304)   (14,147)   (33,566)   (20,270)</p>
<p>Net loss per share   (1.61)     (1.76)     (2.66)     (2.65)</p>
<p>Weighted average common shares outstanding</p>
<p>		     12,618	8,404     12,601	7,657 (1)</p>
<p>(In thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: -- Company says took Q2 non-recurring charge of $6.6 million in cash and stock to be issued to cover settlement of the shareholders' lawsuit in 1997.  In 1996, the costs relate to the terminated Teletouch merger and related financing.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1700))</p>
